s":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizer.java-18478:18622-18442:18463","promptId":"#WNGXM","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":18478,"endPos":18622,"startLine":375,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":377,"endLineOffset":21,"length":145}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":18442,"endPos":18463,"startLine":374,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":374,"endLineOffset":41,"length":22}]}]},{"comment":"The change in `Median.java::Median#surrogate` introduces a conditional check for foldable fields. While this seems reasonable, the fallback to the original implementation (`Percentile`) when the field is not foldable might lead to unexpected behavior if the context assumes that `MvMedian` will always be used. Ensure that this fallback aligns with the expected logic flow and performance characteristics.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java-2365:2469-2586:2775","promptId":"#5NMNF","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Median.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2365,"endPos":2469,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":119,"length":105}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2586,"endPos":2775,"startLine":71,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":73,"endLineOffset":118,"length":190}]}]},{"comment":"The removal of a detailed comment in `LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java::LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests#testMultiCountAllWithFilter` reduces documentation for the test case. While the new comment is more concise, it might be beneficial to retain some level of detail about the expected plan structure for future reference or debugging.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-16491:17141-","promptId":"#KX3JE","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":16491,"endPos":17141,"startLine":373,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":382,"endLineOffset":7,"length":651}],"dstChanges":[]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":103,"line":103,"comment_lines":["[][103]"],"review_comment":["use field.fold() since the field can be an expression such as 1 + 1 and you want to return the surrogate before the rest of the optimizer rules kick in.","Would love to just fold, but folding here is not safe unless we check if this will fold to `null`, first. That would require duplicating logic from `FoldNull`, though, which I\u0027d prefer to avoid.\r\n\r\n(Our evaluators cannot deal with null literals in general, and folding here results in the following exception when running e.g. `count(to_double(null))`:\r\n```\r\nillegal data type [null]\r\norg.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException: illegal data type [null]\r\n\tat __randomizedtesting.SeedInfo.seed([DBCF40F13A40EC92:539B7F2B94BC816A]:0)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.CsvTests.stats.Asdf(stats.csv-spec:1708)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:43)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:39)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.evaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:65)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.toEvaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:105)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.evaluator.mapper.EvaluatorMapper.fold(EvaluatorMapper.java:48)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.EsqlScalarFunction.fold(EsqlScalarFunction.java:30)\r\n```\r\n)","Consider the rare case of count(1+1) - there might be count(1+null). This can be moved to a separate issue though to not block this one.","It makes sense to add more tests to account for these cases where an expression is evaluated, esp. to `null`. I\u0027ll do that in another PR, as this one should be backported to 8.14 as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nThese cases are covered in this PR, it\u0027s just that they result in an extra eval+projection.\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS count(1+null)\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecomes something equivalent to\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS x \u003d count(*)\r\n| EVAL `count(1+null)` \u003d COALESCE(MV_COUNT(1+null), 0) * x\r\n| KEEP `count(1+null)`\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich after folding becomes a multiplication of `count(*)` with 0. If we wanted to, we could further optimize this case to avoid the `count(*)` as well.","Opened a PR with additional tests: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/107888"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","id":37860,"created_at":"2024-04-22T07:12:26Z","original_position":42,"side":"RIGHT","position":42,"submitted_on_commit":"496a2448383e0316baf22f3f3605daee2061682f","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,4 +93,30 @@ public Nullability nullable() {\n     protected TypeResolution resolveType() {\n         return EsqlTypeResolutions.isExact(field(), sourceText(), DEFAULT);\n     }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public Expression surrogate() {\n+        var s \u003d source();\n+        var field \u003d field();\n+\n+        if (field.foldable()) {\n+            if (field instanceof Literal l) {","submitted_line":103},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of `surrogate()` methods in `Count` and `CountDistinct` classes seems to handle constant folding logic for these aggregate functions. However, the commented-out TODO in `#0VTRR` suggests that there is an incomplete normalization strategy for different forms of `COUNT()`. This should be addressed to ensure consistency and correctness across various input forms.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java--3407:4400","promptId":"#0VTRR","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3407,"endPos":4400,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":121,"endLineOffset":5,"length":994}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java--2569:2588","promptId":"#MHTBK","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2569,"endPos":2588,"startLine":43,"startLineOffset":96,"endLine":43,"endLineOffset":115,"length":20}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expres